newfs_udf/makefs -t udf: udf_set_regid strcpy overruns regid.id by one byte

"*UDF Metadata Partition" and "*UDF Sparable Partition" are exactly 23
characters, the size of regid.id, so strcpy writes its NUL into id_suffix[0].
Harmless in the image (already zero), but undefined behaviour, and glibc's
_FORTIFY_SOURCE aborts. Copy at most the field size.

Against NetBSD src 477d71b4d1b73a66b61a03b5f6d3dc9212d4f888 (sbin/newfs_udf/udf_core.c v1.14). Apply with patch -p1
in the src tree. Details: BUG-REPORT.md, bug 2.

--- a/sbin/newfs_udf/udf_core.c
+++ b/sbin/newfs_udf/udf_core.c
@@ -775,7 +775,8 @@
 {
 	memset(regid, 0, sizeof(*regid));
 	regid->flags    = 0;		/* not dirty and not protected */
-	strcpy((char *) regid->id, name);
+	/* ids may fill the field exactly ("*UDF Metadata Partition" is 23 of 23 bytes): no NUL */
+	memcpy(regid->id, name, MIN(strlen(name), sizeof(regid->id)));
 }
 
 
